Fix the build of search5/navidrome@feat-podcast-ux-improvements/5420
(upstream PR navidrome/navidrome#5949, HEAD 07cf48cb).

The branch calls validateURL() in core/podcasts/podcasts.go at lines 315 and 539
but never defines it, so the image cannot be built:

    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:8:2:    "net" imported and not used
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:10:2:   "net/url" imported and not used
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:315:12: undefined: validateURL
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:539:12: undefined: validateURL

The function was never deleted -- it was never written. Four commits made within
65 seconds on 2026-09-07, all through the GitHub web editor, add the pieces
around it and nothing else:

    cb193a0e8a  adds the "net" and "net/url" imports
    037fcfd8d7  adds the call in fetchAndParse
    a2aaf3e9d6  puts /podcast/preview behind adminOnlyMiddleware
    07cf48cb8c  adds the call in doDownload

That burst is a security hardening pass: restrict the preview endpoint, validate
URLs before server-side fetches. So an SSRF guard was clearly the intent, which
is also why "net" is imported.

There is no reusable helper in the tree. conf.validateURL (conf/configuration.go:906)
is unexported and takes a different signature; the plugin host client's check is a
method on httpServiceImpl coupled to per-plugin permissions. core/artwork/agent_images.go:35
rolls its own inline. A local function is therefore what the codebase convention calls for.

The reconstruction below mirrors both precedents: scheme and host checks from
conf.validateURL, address check from isPrivateOrLoopback in plugins/host_httpclient.go.
Like that one it only inspects IP literals, so it does not stop DNS rebinding.

KNOWN: this leaves the branch's own suite at 78 passed / 23 failed. Every failure
is this guard rejecting the httptest fixtures on 127.0.0.1. A scheme-only variant
passes 101/101 but implements no SSRF protection; the guard was kept because the
pod's CiliumNetworkPolicy allows egress to `world`, which includes the home LAN.
Neither the Docker build nor pre-commit runs those tests.

NOTE: this file is tab-indented Go source. .pre-commit-config.yaml excludes
